    "text": "Let a tangent to the curve&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>24</mn><mi>x</mi></math> meet the curve&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></math> at the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>. Then the mid-points of such line segments <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;lie on a parabola with the",
    "image": null
  },
